    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so im working with a client who's pretty much stuck on their squat. been at the same weight for like 3 weeks now and they cant seem to move past it. can u explain how doing a deload week or messing with the volume might actually help them break through that plateau?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A deload week allows the central nervous system and muscles to recover from accumulated fatigue, which can be the real limiter causing the stall. By temporarily reducing volume and intensity, you allow for supercompensation, meaning the body bounces back stronger than before the plateau. Experimenting with volume, such as slightly increasing reps or decreasing weight in a different rep range, can also introduce a novel stimulus that challenges the muscles in a new way to elicit adaptation.",
      "source": "target",
