    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. i guess im just worried about the psychological side too. it feels like every time they get close to a new PR, they just shut down or lose that drive. is there a biological reason why progress feels so stagnant and \"stuck\" sometimes, or is it just mental?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While mental fatigue is significant, biological plateaus often reflect insufficient recovery or adaptation signals. Progress stalls when the demand placed on the body exceeds its current capacity to repair and strengthen itself. This can be a systemic issue involving energy depletion or adaptation ceilings reached at the current stimulus parameters, not just lack of motivation. Therefore, addressing both physical recovery and psychological frustration often yields the best results.",
      "source": "target",
