    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk it just feels weirdly... unnatural. like they have the strength, but something is actively holding them back or sabotaging them right at the finish line. is there any way to frame the plateau as something more than just \"lack of recovery\"? like is there anything else that can cause that kind of sudden, stubborn stall in progress?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sometimes stalls are related to controlling the exercise mechanics, particularly when under heavy load. Subtle breakdowns in bracing, bar path control, or the specific muscle recruitment pattern can become very apparent when the weight gets heavy, halting progression. Furthermore, changes in systemic factors like sleep quality, stress hormones (cortisol), or minor nutrition deficiencies can sabotage performance even if workouts look identical. Re-evaluating movement quality and overall lifestyle stressors can often uncover the hidden bottleneck.",
      "source": "target",
